From ad6ba8a87c299f639eb95633cbab75aaf2eff2fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:53:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 267/273] drm/atomic-helper: Restore max_bpc default on
 connector reset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property() sets the connector's initial
state to the property's max value, but that only applies to the one
state object that exists at attach time. Every connector goes through
another reset shortly after, from drm_mode_config_reset() at the end
of driver load, which unconditionally replaces every connector's
state via __drm_atomic_helper_connector_state_reset() — and that
helper never touches max_bpc/max_requested_bpc, so they come back
zeroed from the fresh kzalloc'd state.

Since bridges read max_requested_bpc to decide which bus format to
propose (see dw_hdmi_bridge_atomic_get_output_bus_fmts(), which
requires max_bpc >= 10/12/16 before proposing anything above 8-bit),
this silently pins every connector to 8-bit output until userspace
explicitly sets the max bpc property, which most simple boot paths
(fbcon, minimal compositors) never do.

Restore the property's max value on every reset, matching what
drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property() already does once at attach
time. This only affects connectors that have the property attached;
__drm_atomic_helper_connector_state_reset() is only called from the
reset path, never from state duplication, so an explicit userspace
override made during normal operation is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
index cc70508d4fdb..41c918e0ca52 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
@@ -437,7 +437,22 @@ void
 __drm_atomic_helper_connector_state_reset(struct drm_connector_state *conn_state,
 					  struct drm_connector *connector)
 {
+	struct drm_property *prop = connector->max_bpc_property;
+
 	conn_state->connector = connector;
+
+	/*
+	 * drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property() only initializes
+	 * max_bpc/max_requested_bpc on the connector's state at the time
+	 * it is called. drm_mode_config_reset() unconditionally replaces
+	 * every connector's state afterwards, which would otherwise leave
+	 * max_requested_bpc at its zeroed default and permanently prevent
+	 * bridges from ever negotiating above the property's minimum.
+	 */
+	if (prop) {
+		conn_state->max_bpc = prop->values[1];
+		conn_state->max_requested_bpc = prop->values[1];
+	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(__drm_atomic_helper_connector_state_reset);
 
